# WHAT IT COVERS: the 2026-11-12 stream, 95.3 minutes cut to the gameplay its video shows,
# captured through Windows.Graphics.Capture with o:vsync on e6c7c76, and the first capture made
# with the step tolerance on by default (18% for o:vsync when -steptol is not typed: 3000 us,
# easing back 500 us a present). It carries step_tolerance_pct 18, so every arm of the replay
# runs the rule as the relay did. The game hitched (20 to 100 ms) 223 times (140 an hour) and
# stalled for 100 ms or more 33 times (21 an hour), in 88 bursts, 27 of them with a stall; the
# longest stalls are 499 ms at about 4040 s, 492 ms at about 4805 s and 491 ms at about
# 5460 s. No periodic stretch. The lock released 17 times. The worst blend run is 40 presents
# in the field and on the dejitter arm, 44 on the plain arm. At a 100 ms flow gap limit, 195
# synthesized presents over 40 pairs would be drawn as the blend.
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 51.573 s, from the 2345
# marked frames in its first 39 s, matched within 0.41 ms of that offset (p90). The video runs
# 5719.7 s with no holes; it opens on gameplay and ends on gameplay, with the game's sleep wheel
# for about 25 s in its last minute, so the cut is its whole span, 51.6 s to 5771.3 s. Inside
# the cut, 11 seconds in 11 runs fall out of the 60 fps regime, each a single hitch second.
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, with the rule at the setting the key
# names, so the two lines are comparable. The replay line (the plain arm, no dejitter) reads
# synth 0.6% against 0.6%, worst run 44 against 40 (at the 10% limit), runs >= 50 0 against 0
# and pull wraps 61 against 62. On the dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran, the worst run
# is 40, the field's. Counted over the window, replay against field: synthesized presents 2015
# against 2014, repeats 291 against 291, skips 86 against 87. The lock released 17 times in the
# field and 17 on the replay: 14 pairs within 0.44 ms, 2 one present (17 ms) apart, and one
# field-only release at 3824.677 s against a replay-only one at 3825.011 s. The replay makes 62
# moves, 14 of them late, and 14 land more than 2 ms from a real frame; the field made 61 inside
# the window. With the rule off the same replay synthesizes 0.4% against 0.6% as run, with the
# same worst run 40, and its content step is less even: rms over every step 594 us against 572
# as run, steps off by over 2 ms 0.46% against 0.32%.
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
